6. Full Economic Indicator Specification
6.1 Economic Indicator Schema
The economic indicator schema defines the structure of an economic indicator deposit.

It has the following fields:

indicator_id. A string. Required.

indicator_name. A string. Required.

indicator_description. A string. Required.

category. A string. Required.

subcategory. A string. Optional.

definition. An object. Required. It contains statement and formal_definition.

source_data. An array of source objects. Required.

computation_method. An object. Required. It contains formula, transformation, and notes.

assumptions. An array of assumption objects. Required.

known_limitations. An array of limitation objects. Required.

revisions. An array of revision objects. Optional.

base_year. A string. Optional.

reference_period. A string. Optional.

frequency. An enum. Required. The values are daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, annual, other.

seasonal_adjustment. An object. Required. It contains applied and method.

coverage. An object. Required. It contains geographic and demographic.

institutional_source. An object. Required. It contains agency, country, and publication_reference.

related_indicators. An array of indicator relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

verification_result_reference. A string. Optional.

instrument_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each source object has:

source_id. A string.

source_name. A string.

source_type. An enum. The values are survey, administrative_data, transaction_data, satellite_data, estimation, other.

source_reference. A string.

source_description. A string.

frequency. An enum. The values are daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, annual, other.

Each assumption object has:

assumption_id. A string.

assumption_description. A string.

assumption_type. An enum. The values are economic, statistical, methodological, behavioural, institutional, other.

impact_if_wrong. A string.

Each limitation object has:

limitation_id. A string.

limitation_description. A string.

limitation_type. An enum. The values are coverage, measurement, timeliness, comparability, revision, other.

impact. A string.

Each revision object has:

revision_id. A string.

revision_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

revision_description. A string.

previous_definition. A string.

new_definition. A string.

reason. A string.

institutional_source. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each indicator relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_indicator_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are alternative, complement, component, derivative, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

