7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Economic Indicator
function createEconomicIndicator(indicator, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the indicator against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the verification result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. If the instrument reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. Generate an indicator ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 7. Insert the economic indicator.

Step 8. Insert the source records, the assumption records, the limitation records, the revision records, and the indicator relations.

Step 9. Insert the work link, the verification link, and the instrument link if present.

Step 10. Insert the provenance.

Step 11. Insert the moderation record.

Step 12. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 13. Return the indicator_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Economic Indicator
function readEconomicIndicator(indicatorId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the indicator. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the sources, the assumptions, the limitations, the revisions, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Economic Indicator
function updateEconomicIndicator(indicatorId, indicator, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing indicator. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new indicator.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the indicator_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Economic Indicator
function deleteEconomicIndicator(indicatorId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing indicator. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the indicator_id and the status deleted.

